  "question": {
    "text": "The excess pressure inside a soap bubble A in air is half the excess pressure inside another soap bubble B in air. If the volume of the bubble A is $n$ times the volume of the bubble $B$, then, the value of $n$ is ___.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\Delta \\mathrm{P}=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{~T}}{\\mathrm{R}} \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{B}}}=\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}}{\\Delta \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}}}=2 \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{~V}_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{B}}}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{B}}}\\right)^3=8\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
